        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Adirondack Mountains, New York, Quebec, Canada\n- Topics: Deicke bentonite layer, Millbrig bentonite layer, geologic era, effects\n\nFacts:\n- The Adirondack Mountains are identified in relation to the area between New York and Quebec, Canada.\n- The chunk states that the Adirondack Mountains were the most affected location between New York and Quebec, Canada, during the era when the Deicke and Millbrig bentonite layers were formed.\n- The Deicke bentonite layer and the Millbrig bentonite layer were formed during the same referenced geologic era.",
